# FloqAi venue search (Search for page)

Resume: `@venue-search$` / `$floqai-search$` / `@near-me$`.

This is **search**, not help. Help copy (`?`, FloqAi repository bodies) never explains the parser.

## Page contract (`index.html#categoryPage`)

- **No** "Search for" heading and **no** Events / Clubs / Beach Clubs / Lounges / Lounge-Clubs tiles (removed s3.0.106 — FloqAi search replaces them). Below the search: `Or` + product tiles (ShoutOut, Mingl, BartR, RydR, supRstar, FloqAi).
- FloqAi mark + dialog are **stationary above** the search input (`#categoryFloqAiSearch`). Mark is animated (bob + glow + halo; faster `is-listening` while typing). Dialog is **borderless, unframed** text beside the mark with a type-on reveal (`is-speaking`, clip-path; RTL mirrored). `prefers-reduced-motion` disables all of it.
- Dialog loop (5s, only while input is empty and the page is active): `cat.floqaiWelcome` ("Welcome, type below to search for Events") → `cat.floqaiAlso` ("You may also search for: Clubs or Lounges").
- While typing, the dialog shows the live interpretation: `cat.floqaiSearching` ("Searching {type}") · genres · `cat.floqaiIn` ("in {place}") or `cat.floqaiNearYou` ("near you"). `data-i18n` is removed while it shows a live interpretation so `applyText` does not overwrite it.
- Submit → `showAdSplash(type)` → `openVenueSearch(type, query)` → listing opens with that type and `#locationSearch` prefilled.

## Parser (`floqr-venue-query.js` → `window.FLOQRVenueQuery`)

- `normalize`: NFD, strip diacritics, `&` → "and", split on non-letters/digits. Word lookup compacts spans (max 4 tokens), so `Beachclub`, `Beach club`, `Beach-club`, `Beach clubs`, `beach_clubs` share one key. Singular fallback strips trailing `s`/`es`.
- `VENUE_TYPES` word lists: `events`, `beach-clubs`, `lounge-club`, `lounges`, `clubs` (English variants + all supported languages). Add new spellings **only** to the `words` array for that type; tests cover variants.
- Type precedence: **events wins** over venue words. Otherwise most specific: lounge-club > beach-clubs > lounges > clubs.
- Entry context: `parse(q, {entry})`. Search for page defaults to `events`. On a listing page the listing's own type wins **unless** the query names another type (`typeSource === "query"`).
- `NEAR_ME` phrases (all 11 languages: near me, nearby, closest, cerca de mí, près de moi, in der Nähe, vicino a me, perto de mim, рядом, κοντά μου, w pobliżu, in de buurt, بالقرب مني …) set `nearMe: true` and are **not** a place. An explicit place wins (`nearMe` is false when `place` is set).
- `GENRES` / `PLACES` are stripped; only `residual` goes to `floqrSearch`. Records are strictly filtered with `matchesFilters(parsed, record, extraText)`.
- Free-text place: words after the last `PLACE_PREPOSITIONS` token, stopping at `WHEN_WORDS` / "this" / "next". Unknown cities ("Clubs in Accra") match record text, so **new cities need no word-list change**; `PLACES` only adds aliases (DC, NYC, Monte Carlo).

## Location-aware order (default for every listing search)

Rule (product): **GPS first, then IP**, then profile city. Results are **nearest to the user first, then name A→Z**. No user location → name A→Z.

| Query | Filter | Order |
|---|---|---|
| No place ("EDM clubs", "EDM clubs near me") | type + genre | distance from user (GPS → IP → profile), then name |
| With place ("Clubs in Monaco") | type + genre + place | distance from user (GPS → IP → profile), then name; same-city venues tie on whole km → name |

- `floqr-geo-search.js` → `window.FLOQRGeoSearch` (UMD, node-tested): `resolveUserLocation`, `sortNearest`, `recordCoordinates`, `parseIpPayload`.
- GPS: `navigator.geolocation` with a 3s wait. If the permission prompt answers later, `onLateGps` fires `floqr:location-updated`; `patron-app.js` resets the context and re-renders the listing.
- IP: default provider `https://get.geojs.io/v1/ip/geo.json` (no key, CORS). Override with `window.FLOQR_IP_GEOLOCATION_PROVIDER = "https://…"`; `false` disables. Only city/region/country/lat/lng are cached (`sessionStorage["floqr.ipLocation.v1"]`, 6h) — **never the IP address**. Disclosed in `privacy.html`.
- `ai-location-service.js` `getUserLocationContext` delegates to `FLOQRGeoSearch` (`locationSource: gps|ip|profile|unknown`, `locationCity`). Works signed out.
- Listings: `sortListingNearest` in `patron-app.js` (events use event coords, else the venue's). Status line keys: `listing.sortNearest` / `listing.sortByName` / `listing.source*` / `listing.yourLocation`.
- Distance is straight-line (haversine) on the device. Google Distance Matrix is **not** called per search (cost, key exposure).

## Venue coordinates — Google, zero code per new city

- `functions/venue-geocode-functions.js`: `onClubLocationGeocode` (Firestore `clubLocations/{id}` write) + `scheduledVenueGeocodeBackfill` (every 12h, ≤60 per run). Uses the existing `GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY` secret: Places API (New) Text Search `places.location`, fallback Geocoding API.
- Writes top-level `latitude` / `longitude` + `geo {signature, source, formattedAddress, placeId, geocodedAt}`. `geo.signature` = normalized address/city query; unchanged signature → no re-geocode (loop-safe). Address change → re-geocode. `google-miss` recorded once per signature. `geoManual: true` or `geo.source: "manual"` → never overwritten.
- Client `recordCoordinates` order: stored lat/lng (any of `latitude/longitude`, `lat/lng`, `geo`, `location`, `coordinates`) → built-in city table fallback (seed data only). New clubs in new cities sort correctly as soon as the trigger stamps coordinates.
- Contract tests: `functions/venue-geocode-core.test.js`, `functions/floqr-geo-search.test.js`.

## Native apps (later — not buildable in the web app today)

- iOS Core Location / Android Fused Location Provider: request **When In Use** only; precise optional (approximate is enough for sorting). Reuse `sortNearest` semantics (distance then name) so web and native agree.
- Cache last fix ~10 min; re-sort on significant change (>1 km) instead of polling.
- Optional server search: store `geohash` alongside lat/lng in the geocode trigger and query by geohash ranges when venue counts outgrow client-side sorting (~5k+).
- Optional radius filter for "near me" (e.g. 50 km, widen if empty) — only after venue coordinates are backfilled everywhere.
- Deep links / universal links target `https://www.floqr.com` (see `cutoffrequirement.mdc`).
- Privacy: native permission strings must match `privacy.html` (location used to list nearby events; not stored on profile).

## FloqAi global search (`intent-search.js`)

`venueSearchIntent` runs before help scoring when `isVenueQuery` is true and the query is not help-like. It links to `./?start=search&q=<query>`; `runStartVenueQuery` reads `q`, removes it with `replaceState`, and submits it through the page search path.

## Landing / auth routing

- Landing paragraph lives in the Welcome `?` (`help-welcome`). Location help is `help-location-search` beside the static "Location-aware search" label on the listing page (the title / intro / status lines are rewritten by JS, so the `?` must not attach to them).
- Signed-in users **never** see a Continue / Sign out interstitial. `localStorage["floqr.signedInHint"]` + `html.floqr-auth-resolving` hide landing auth chrome until auth resolves (8s failsafe). `backToWelcomeBtn` hidden while signed in.

